flowchart TB
  accTitle: C4 L1 - Support Bridge system context
  accDescr: Support and engineering work in their source systems. An escalation operator reviews exact changes in Support Bridge. Roles do not establish separate authenticated identities.
  Support["Support engineer<br/>[Person / functional role]<br/>Owns customer escalation and new internal replies"]:::person
  Engineer["Software engineer<br/>[Person / functional role]<br/>Investigates issues and records engineering updates"]:::person
  Operator["Escalation operator<br/>[Person / functional role]<br/>Inspects conflicts and reviews exact state plans"]:::person
  Zendesk["Zendesk Support<br/>[External software system]<br/>Customer tickets and internal notes"]:::external
  GitHub["GitHub Issues<br/>[External software system]<br/>Engineering issues and comments"]:::external
  Bridge["Support Bridge<br/>[Software system in scope]<br/>Tagged intake, durable field reconciliation,<br/>conversation delivery and operator visibility"]:::system

  Support -->|"Tags reports and adds internal context"| Zendesk
  Engineer -->|"Investigates, comments and closes issues"| GitHub
  Operator -->|"Inspects evidence and explicitly approves plans"| Bridge
  Bridge -->|"Reads reports and notes; updates fields<br/>and appends internal engineering notes"| Zendesk
  Bridge -->|"Creates linked issues; updates fields<br/>and appends internal support replies"| GitHub
  Support -->|"Views linked-pair progress"| Bridge

  Legend["Key: dark = person; blue = our software system; grey = external system.<br/>Each arrow describes a directed interaction. Source text and dashboards confer no approval."]:::key

